nf_tables: keep the per-namespace state in net_generic storage

Microsoft's kernel is configured without CONFIG_NF_TABLES, so struct net
has no "nft" member: net_namespace.h only adds struct netns_nftables when
CONFIG_NF_TABLES or CONFIG_NF_TABLES_MODULE is set. Modules built out of
tree against that kernel must see the same struct net as the built-in
code, so net->nft cannot be used. Register the state as pernet generic
data (as upstream did in 5.13 with nft_pernet()) and reach it through
nft_pernet(net). The generation helpers in nf_tables.h were guarded by
IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NF_TABLES); the guard goes, since this copy of the
header is only used to build these modules.

